## Factual data

- `nespal.h` — the widely used NES NTSC 64-colour palette (values generated from the standard NTSC decoding formula; close to Nestopia/FCEUX defaults).
- The VRC7 built-in instrument table in `cart.c` (`opll_inst`) reproduces the patch ROM of the VRC7 chip itself (via emu2413).

Note: the ES1371 sound driver (es1371snd, maintained in its own repository) is a separate work distributed separately under GPL-2.0 — see its `LICENSE` and the header of its `src/main.c`. It is not part of the MIT-licensed BeFC application.
